## API contract

The front calls the API through `useApi()`, typed by `openapi.json`. After any change to a route
or a schema of the backend, `kiln contract` exports `openapi.json` from the Django code, then
regenerates `frontend/app/types/api.d.ts`. Both files are committed with the change; CI fails
when they drift from the code.

{% endif -%}
## Update

On a dedicated branch, with a clean tree: `kiln update` (compatible upgrades) or
`kiln update --major` (major versions too). It brings kiln's improvements without overwriting
local changes, upgrades the dependencies, then runs the checks. With Claude Code, the
`/kiln:update` skill does it all: the kiln tool, then the repo.

